$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Bromination of oxime esters If-Ii and Ve. a. A solution of 0.2 ml of
bromine in 2 ml of CHCl3 or AcOH was added dropwise under vigorous
stirring to a solution of 0.4 g of compound If-Ii in 2 ml of the same
solvent, maintaining the temperature in the range from 20 to 40°C. After
24 h, the precipitate was filtered off and recrystallized. The following
product was obtained: in CHCl3 : IIIf (91%). Mp (solvent: i-PrOH): 74°C;
Formula: C13H11Br2NO4S.
