$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Chlorination of compounds Ia, Ib, Vb, VIa,
VIb, VIIIa, VIIIb, XIaXIc, XIIa-XIIc, XXa-XXc, XXXa, XXXb, XXXIa-XXXIc,
XXXVIIa, and XXXVIIb ( general procedure ). A stream of dry chlorine was
passed at a flow rate of 15-20 ml/min through a solution of 2 mmol of the
corresponding substrate in 3 ml of chloroform, acetic acid,
dimethylformamide, or DMF-AcOH (1:5), maintained at 25-30°C. The amount
of chlorine was controlled by the gain in weight; it was varied from 1 to
3 equiv. After 24 h, the precipitate was filtered off and recrystallized
from acetic acid. The melting points and analytical data are given below
only for products isolated as individual substances. Compound XXIIb.
Yield 91%. mp 142-143°C. 1H NMR spectrum, δ, ppm: 2.24 s (3H, Me), 6.66 s
(1H, 5-H), 7.39-7.94 d.d (4H, C6H4), 2.49 s (3H, MeC6H4). 13C NMR
spectrum, δC, ppm: 174.83 (C1), 135. 83 (C2), 146.46 (C3), 17.02 (3-Me),
164.68 (C4), 58. 64 (C5), 81.63 (C6). Found, %: Cl 34.05, 34.15.
C14H11Cl4NO3S. Calculated, %: Cl 34.16.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Halogenation of N-substituted p-quinone imines and p-quinone oxime
esters: IV. Chlorination and bromination of
