$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: The synthesis of 1,2-dibromocyclohexane is
representative. Sodium bromide (3.06g, 30.0 mmol) is added to mixture of
sodium perborate (2.29g, 15.0 mmol) and cyclohexene (1.11g, 13.5 mmol) in
glacial acetic acid (25 ml) and stirred for 2 h. The mixture is then
diluted with water, the product extracted into ether and dried over
MgSO4. Removal of solvent followed by column chromatography (silica gel,
hexanes) gives 1,2-dibromocyclohexane in 87% yield. 1,2-Dibromooctane.
Yield 83%. bp(lit)°C: 242-243 (52@15 Torr); 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ ppm: 4.18
(m, 1H), 3.85 (dd, 1H), 3.62 (t, 1H), 211 (m, 1H), 175 (m, 1H), 1.52 (m,
1H), 1.28 (s, 7H), 0.88 (t, 3H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Bromination of alkenes using a mixture of sodium bromide and sodium
perborate
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kabalka, G. W.; Yang, K.; Reddy, N. K.; Narayana, C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (1998), 28(5), 925-929

