$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1,2-Dibromooctane, 5. C60Br8 (100 mg, 0.074 mmol) was dissolved in 30mL
of 1,1,2,2-tetrachloroethane followed by the addition of 1-octene (1 mL).
The solution was heated to 90°C for 12 hours. The reaction mixture was
cooled to room temperature and all volatiles removed. The residue was
chromatographed on a silica column using hexane as the eluent. 16.5 mg,
82%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM C60Cl6, C60Br8 and C60(NO2)6 as selective tools in organic synthesis
