$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The synthesis of (E)-1,2-dibromooctene is representative. Sodium bromide
(1.03 g, 10.0 mmol) was added to the mixture of sodium perborate (1.54 g,
10.0 mmol) and 1-octyne (0.55 g, 5.0 mmol) in glacial acetic acid (25 ml)
and stirred for 1.5 hr. The mixture was then extracted into CCl4 (10 mL),
washed with H2O (10 mL) and dried over anhydrous MgSO4 · The yield was
89.7% as measured by 1H NMR using 1,4-dioxane as an internal standard.
(E)-1,2-dibromooctene, yield 89.7%. The product had a boiling point of
112°C @ 7.8 Torr (Lit. 89-92° @ 3 Torr)3. 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ ppm: 6.39 (s,
1H), 2.60 (t, 2H), 1.58(m, 2H), 1.32 (m, 6H), 0.91 (t, 3H)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Bromination of alkynes with sodium perborate and sodium bromide
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kabalka, G. W.; Yang, K.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (1998), 28(20), 3807-3809

