$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Bromination of 16. A solution of 16 (0.17 g, 1.0 mmol) in CH2- Cl2 (2 mL)
was treated dropwise with bromine until an orange color persisted. The
solvent was evaporated under vacuum, and the residue was purified by
column chromatography on silica gel (elution with 70:30 hexanes/EtOAc) to
provide a mixture of the isomeric dibromides 26 and 27 (0.30 g, 90%): 26
and 27, yield (0.30 g, 90%) IR (CH2Cl2,cm-1) 1342, 1170, 1140; 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 4.87 (ddd, J = 6.8, 10.4, 11.6 Hz, 1H (L)), 4.78 (ddd,
J = 6.8, 9.6, 11.6 Hz, 1H (M)), 4.37-4.28 (m, 1H (L), 1H (M)), 4.17 (dd,
J = 6.8, 15.2 Hz, 1H (M)), 3.95 (dd, J = 11.6, 15.2 Hz, 1H (L)),
3.87-3.80 (m, 1H (M)), 3.72 (dd, J = 3.6, 15.2 Hz, 1H (L)), 3.62-3.50 (m,
2H (L)), 3.36-3.28 (m, 2H (M)), 3.22-3.12 (m, 2H (L), 1H (M)), 2.87- 2.72
(m, 1H (L), 2H (M)), 2.63-2.54 (m, 1H (M)), 2.30-2.24 (m, 1H (L)),
2.22-2.11 (m, 1H (L), 1H (M)); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 58.0, 56.1,
54.3, 53.5, 52.9, 52.7, 51.9, 50.4, 49.4, 43.0, 41.2, 39.9, 32.0, 24.5 (M
) more dominant; L ) less dominant).
