$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Bromination of ammonium salts Ia-Id,
IIIa-IIId, V, and VI. To aqueous solution of 0.03 mol of salt Ia-Id,
IIIa-IIId, V, or VI we added dropwise at room temperature with constant
stirring a 10- or 5-fold molar amount of bromine. After 4 h, the complex
that formed was washed with water (5 x 50 ml) and dried. Decomposition
with acetone (chemical grade) gave compound IIa-IId, IVa-g, VII, or VIII
as hygroscopic oily or crystalline substances. They were recrystallized
from absolute ethanol. Comp. no.: VII, Yield: 90%. Rf : 0.57, IR
spectrum, v, cm-1: 1645, 2260, Formula: C19H35Br2ClN2. 1H NMR spectrum
[CD3OD or (CD3)2SO], δ, ppm (J, Hz): 1.31 t and 1.44 t (15H, CH2CH3, J
8.0), 3.39 q and 3.51 q (10H, CH2CH3), 4.24 d (2H, CH2CH=, J 4.2), 4.38 s
(2H, CH2CCl=), 4.48 s (2H, CH2C≡), 5.68 d.d (1H, =CH-H, J 1 10.8, J 2
2.4), 5.82 d.d (1H, =CH-H, J 1 17.8, J 2 2.4), 5.92 d.d.t (1H, CH=CH2, J
1 17.8, J 2 10.8, J 3 2.4), 6.44 br.t (1H, CH=CCl, J 5.5).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
