$DATUM 1.2-Dibromo-2,2-dichloroethyl propyl sulfide (II). To a solution of 3.4 g
of 2,2-dichlorovinyl propyl sulfide (I) in 20 ml of CCl4, cooled to 0°C,
we added with stirring 1.05 ml of bromine (dropwise), and the mixture was
stirred for 30 min at room temperature. The solvent was removed, and the
residue was distilled under reduced pressure. Yield 6 g (90%). bp 85-95°C
(1 mm), n D 20 1.5600. 1H NMR spectrum (90 MHz), δ, ppm: 5,61 s (1H,
CHBr), 2.95 t (SCH2), 1.77 m (CH2), 1.07 t (CH3). Found %: C 18.57; H
2.82; Br 48.17; Cl 21.76; S 10.21. C5H8Br2Cl2S. Calculated, %: C 18.15; H
2.44; Br 48.30; Cl 21.43; S 9.69.
