$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The synthesis of 1,2-dibromocyclohexane is representative. Sodium bromide
(3.06g, 30.0 mmol) is added to mixture of sodium perborate (2.29g, 15.0
mmol) and cyclohexene (1.11g, 13.5 mmol) in glacial acetic acid (25 ml)
and stirred for 2 h. The mixture is then diluted with water, the product
extracted into ether and dried over MgSO4. Removal of solvent followed by
column chromatography (silica gel, hexanes) gives 1,2-dibromocyclohexane
in 87% yield. 1,2-dibromocyclohexane. Yield 87%. mp. 230-231 °C;
bp(lit)°C: 230-231 (99.6-99.9@13 Torr); 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ ppm: 4.45 (t,
2H), 2.46 (m, 2H), 1.82 (m, 4H), 1.05 (m, 2H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Bromination of alkenes using a mixture of sodium bromide and sodium
perborate
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kabalka, G. W.; Yang, K.; Reddy, N. K.; Narayana, C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (1998), 28(5), 925-929

