$DATUM 64-19-7
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
2-(1,2-Dibromo-2-phenylethyl)-4-oxo-4H-1-benzopyrans 13a,b and
2-(1,2-Dibromo-2-phenylethyl)-4-oxo-4H-1-benzo[b]thiopheno[3,2-b]pyran
(17) To a stirred solution of 12a, 12b, or 16 (0.002 mol) in acetic acid
(3 ml) was added dropwise over a period of 20 min a solution of bromine
(0.003 mol) in 5 ml of acetic acid. The mixture was then stirred for 3 h,
and the white precipitate formed was filtered off, washed with acetic
acid (5 mI), and recrystallized from the proper solvent to give compounds
13a,b and 17 respectively. Compound 13b, yield 89%. M.P.(°C): 225;
Solvent: AcOH; Molecular formula: C17H11Br2NO4; (MW): (453); IR (ν,
cm-1): 1640 (C=O δ-pyrone), 1085 (C-Br)
