$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for
(2Z,4Z)-Methyl-2-(bromomethyl)-5-chloro-5-(3-chlorophenyl)penta-2,4-dienoate
(5a) Br2 (1.60 g, 10.0 mmol) was added dropwise to a stirring solution of
Ph3P (2.62 g, 10.0 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (20 mL) at 0 °C, followed by dropwise
addition of a solution of 4a (2.87 g, 10.0 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (10 mL). The
reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for 15 min. Then the
reaction was quenched by 20% Na2S2O3 solution (5 mL) and extracted with
CH2Cl2 (3x30 mL). The combined organic phase was dried over Na2SO4 and
evaporated under reduced pressure to give a crude product, which was
purified by flash-column chromatography on silica gel (petroleum
ether/ethyl acetate=20:1) to give 89% yield of 5a (3.12 g).
(Z)-Ethyl-2-(bromomethyl)-3-(1-chloro-3,4-dihydronaphthalen-2-yl)acrylate
(5l). Yellow solid, yield 89%. mp 61.6-62.4°C. IR (KBr) νmax: 3132, 1708,
1399, 1287 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.86 (1H, s, ClC=CCH=C),
7.67-7.69 (1H, m, ArH), 7.27-7.29 (2H, m, ArH), 7.16-7.18 (1H, m, ArH),
4.30-4.39 (4H, s, CH2Br and CO2CH2CH3), 2.85-2.92 (4H, m, CH2CH2), 1.37
(3H, t, J 11.6 Hz, CO2CH2CH3); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 166.0, 140.3,
136.7, 134.6, 132.3, 130.4, 129.4, 129.2, 127.0, 126.9, 125.6, 61.4,
27.9, 27.7, 26.3, 14.2; MS (EI) m/z 356.0 (M++2, 2), 319.0 (18), 275.1
(28), 241.1 (33), 165.1 (100), 128.1 (15); HRMS (EI) m/z calcd. for
C16H16BrClO2: 354.0022; found: 354.0017.
