$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Bromination of oxime esters If-Ii and Ve. a. A
solution of 0.2 ml of bromine in 2 ml of CHCl3 or AcOH was added dropwise
under vigorous stirring to a solution of 0.4 g of compound If-Ii in 2 ml
of the same solvent, maintaining the temperature in the range from 20 to
40°C. After 24 h, the precipitate was filtered off and recrystallized.
Compound: IIIg (89%).
5,6-dibromo-4-(4-chloro-phenylsulfonyloxyimino)-3-methyl-2-cyclohexenone
(IIIg). 13C NMR spectrum, δC, ppm: 187.03 (C=O), 157.34 (C=N), 145.15 (C4
in ArSO2), 142.09 (C3), 133.35 (C1 in ArSO2), 130.81 (C3 in ArSO2),
129.97 (C2 in ArSO2), 129.59 (C2), 43.62 (C5), 34.43 (C6), 18.49 (Me). Mp
(solvent: i-PrOH): 145°C; Formula: C13H10Br2ClNO4S.
