$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: The synthesis of (E)-1,2-dibromooctene is
representative. Sodium bromide (1.03 g, 10.0 mmol) was added to the
mixture of sodium perborate (1.54 g, 10.0 mmol) and 1-octyne (0.55 g, 5.0
mmol) in glacial acetic acid (25 ml) and stirred for 1.5 hr. The mixture
was then extracted into CCl4 (10 mL), washed with H2O (10 mL) and dried
over anhydrous MgSO4 · The yield was 89.7% as measured by 1H NMR using
1,4-dioxane as an internal standard. (E)-3.4-dibromohexene, yield 85.3%.
b.p. (lit)°C: 32°@7.4 Torr (30@7.1 ° Torr3); 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ ppm: 2.64
(q, 4H), 1.11 (t, 6H)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Bromination of alkynes with sodium perborate and sodium bromide
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kabalka, G. W.; Yang, K.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (1998), 28(20), 3807-3809

