$DATUM Methyl
1-(2,3-dibromopropyl)-4-hydroxy-2,2-dioxo-1H-2λ6,1-benzothiazine-3-carboxylate
(IV). A solution of I (2.95 g, 0.01 mol) in glacial HOAc (10 mL) was
stirred vigorously and treated with a solution of Br2 (0.52 mL, 0.01 mol)
in the same solvent (5 mL). The brown Br2 color faded immediately. The
reaction mixture was diluted with cold H2O. The resulting precipitate was
filtered off, rinsed with cold H2O, and dried. Yield 3.96 g (87%). mp
123-125°C (Et2O). PMR spectrum, δ, ppm (J, Hz): 13.21 (s, 1H, OH); 8.01
(d, 1H, J = 8.0, H-5); 7.76 (t, 1H, J = 7.7, H-7); 7.63 (d, 1H, J = 8.3,
H-8); 7.41 (t, 1H, J = 7.6, H-6); 4.60-4.35 (m, 3H, NCH2CHBr); 3.95 (d,
2H, J = 4.0, CH 2Br); 3.88 (s, 3H, OMe). C13H13Br2NO5S. Crystals of IV
(C13H13Br2NO5S, MW 455.12) were triclinic (Et2O), at 20°C a = 8.384(1); b
= 9.145(1); c = 11.246(2) Å; α = 68.13(1)°; β = 89.11(1)°; γ = 87.14(1)°;
V = 799.3(2) Å3; MW = 455.12; Z = 2; space group P1; d calc = 1.891
g/cm3; μ(MoKα) = 1.891 mm-1; F(000) = 448.
