$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Bromination of Dimethyl
7-oxabicyclo[2.2.1]hept-2,5-diene-2,3-dicarboxylate (10) at -60°C:
Synthesis of Dimethyl trans-5,
6-Dibromo-7-oxabicyclo[2.2.1]-hept-2-ene-2,3-dicarboxylate (11). To a
magnetically stirred solution of dicarboxylate 10 (500 mg, 2.38 mmol) in
20 mL dry chloroform cooled to-60°C was added dropwise a solution of
bromine (419 mg, 2.62 mmol) in 5 mL chloroform for 10 minutes. After
stirring for 5 minutes at-60°C, the solution was slowly warmed to room
temperature. After removal of the solvent under reduced pressure, the
oily residue was chromatographed over silica gel (20 g) with carbon
tetrachloride as the eluent to give product. Yield: 770 mg (87%) of
dibromide 11, pale, yellow viscous oil. 1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3) δ 5.39
(dd, J= 4.4, 1.1 Hz, 1H, H6), 5.21 (d, J= 1.1 Hz, 1H, H5), 4.28 (dd, J=
4.4 and 2.4 Hz, 1H, H1), 3.97 (d, J= 2.4 Hz, 1H, H4), 3.81 (s, 3H), 3.76
(s, 3H). 13C NMR (50 MHz, CDCl3) δ 164.2, 162.7, 145.5, 144.5, 90.6,
85.5, 54.7, 54.6, 51.3, 50.3. IR (KBr, cm-1): 3004, 2948, 2852, 1727,
1619, 1442, 1312, 1217, 1147, 1106,1036, 1005, 943, 889.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM High-temperature bromination XIII [1]: bromination of dimethyl
7-oxabicyclo[2.2.1]hepta-2,5-diene-2,3-dicarboxylate
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Simsek, Nermin; Arici, Cengiz; McKee, Michael L.; Ulku, Dincer; Balci,
Metin
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Structural Chemistry (2001), 12(3/4), 305-311

