$DATUM 6.2.2 Conversion of 4-tert-butyl cyclohexene (2a) with aqueous H2O2 / HBr
in dimethyl carbonate. Reagents: 4-tert-butyl cyclohexene (2a) (1 mmol),
aq. H2O2 [30% (w/w), 2.5 eq.], aq. HBr [48% (w/w), 2.5 eq.], DMC (10 mL).
Mixing of the reagents at 20°C, stirring of the reaction mixture for 24 h
at the same temperature, solvent evaporation and column chromatography.
rel-(1R,3S, 4S)-3,4-dibromo-1-tert-butyl cyclohexane (3a), yield 86%.
