$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Bromination of β-aroylacrylic acids. A
solution of 0.05 mol of bromine in 10 mL of chloroform was added to a
solution of 0.05 mol of β-aroylacrylic acid in 25-30 mL of chloroform
within 3 h under vigorous stirring at room temperature. The crystals
formed were filtered off, washed with chloroform, and dried in a vacuum.
Characteristics of the obtained compounds Ia-Id are given in Tables 1 and
2. β-aroyl-α,β-dibromopropionic acid 1d. Yield: 86.23%. Formula:
C10H7Br3O3, mp: 152-153°C, Found: C: 28.66%, H: 1.74%, Br: 57.76%,
Calculated: C: 28.92%, H: 1.69%, Br: 57.83%. 1H NMR (DMSO-d6+CCl4, 1 :
3): δ, ppm 4.70 d (1H, CH, J1 0.1 Hz), 5.71 d (1H, CH, J1 0.1 Hz),
7.66-7.71 m (2H, C6H4), 7.96-8.01 m (2H, C6H4), 9.72 br.s (1H, COOH).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of β-aroylvinyl derivatives of triphenylphosphine and pyridine
based on β-aroylacrylic acids
