$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Bromination of ammonium salts Ia-Id, IIIa-IIId, V, and VI. To aqueous
solution of 0.03 mol of salt Ia-Id, IIIa-IIId, V, or VI we added dropwise
at room temperature with constant stirring a 10- or 5-fold molar amount
of bromine. After 4 h, the complex that formed was washed with water (5 x
50 ml) and dried. Decomposition with acetone (chemical grade) gave
compound IIa-IId, IVa-g, VII, or VIII as hygroscopic oily or crystalline
substances. They were recrystallized from absolute ethanol. Comp. no.:
IIa, Yield: 86%. Rf : 0.63, IR spectrum, v, cm-1: 570, 1605, 1610, UV
spectrum, λmax, nm: 223, Formula: C11H16Br6ClN. 1H NMR spectrum [CD3OD or
(CD3)2SO], δ, ppm (J, Hz): 3.34 s (6H, NCH3), 4.28 br.d (2H, NCH2CH=, J
5.5), 3.96 m (2H, CHBrCH2Br), 4.38 s (2H, CH2Br), 4.70 and 4.90 d.d (2H,
CH2CBr=, J gem 15.0), 5.80 d.d (1H, CHBr, J 1 10.8, J 2 5.7), 6.62 t (1H,
CH=CCl, J 5.7).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Bromination of mono- and bisammonium salts with a 4-penten-2-ynyl side
group
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Saakyan, T. A.; Gyul'nazaryan, A. Kh.; Kocharyan, S. T.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Russian Journal of General Chemistry (Translation of Zhurnal Obshchei
Khimii) (2001), 71(8), 1165-1168

