$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1-(But-2-en-1-yl)-2,3-dimethylbenzene and
1-(but-2-en-1-yl)-3,4-dimethylbenzene (If). Buta-1,3-diene, 27 g (0.5
mol), was passed at a flow rate of 6 l/h through a mixture of 160 g (1.5
mol) of 1,2-imethylbenzene and 18.5 g of 86% H3PO4. The mixture was
stirred for 3.5 h at 60°C and treated as described above, and the residue
was distilled under reduced pressure. From 16 g (0.1 mol) of compound Ih.
2-(2,3-Dibromobutyl)-1,4-dimethylbenzene (IIh), yield 27.5 g, 86%. bp
160°C (15 mm), d204 = 1.4943, n20D = 1.5734. IR spectrum: ν 678 cm-1
(C-Br). 1H NMR spectrum, δ, ppm: 6.75-6.87 m (3H, C6H3), 2.34 s (6H,
CH3), 2.88-3.11 d (2H, CH2), 4.0-4.2 m (2H, CHBr), 1.78 s (3H, CH3).
Found, %: C 45.17; H 5.2; Br 51.15. C12H16Br2. Calculated, %: C 45.0; H
5.0; Br 50.0.
