$DATUM N-Butyl(2,3,4,5-tetrabromo-2-pentenyl)amine hydrobromide. To 2 g of
N,N-dibutyl(4-penten-2-ynyl)amine at room temperature we added 4 ml of
40% aqueous hydrobromic acid and then, not isolating the resulting
hydrobromide, 8.2 g of bromine. From the ether extract of the reaction
mixture, butyric aldehyde 2,4-dinitrophenylhydrazone was precipitated, mp
123 °C [2], whose mixture with an authentic sample gave no melting point
depression The structure of this product was confirmed by 1H NMR
spectroscopy. The complex that precipitated was repeatedly washed with
water, dried, and decomposed with acetone of chemically pure grade to
obtain 4.7 g (85%) of N-butyl(2,3,4,5-tetrabromo-2-pentenyl)-amine. mp
134-135°C. 1H NMR spectrum, δ, ppm (J, Hz): 0.97 t (3H, CH2CH3, J 8.0),
1.40 m (2H, CH2CH3), 1.70 m (2H, CH2C2H5), 3.00 m (2H, CH2C3H7), 3.98 m
(2H, CH2C=), 4.32 m and 4.38 m (2H, CH2Br, J gem 14.6), 5.70 d. d (1H,
CHBr, J 1 9.8, J 2 6.1). Found, %: Br- 14.77; N 2.43. M(titr.) 536.
C9H16Br2N. Calculated, %: Br 14.87; N 2.0. M 538.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Dealkylation on bromination of N,N-dibutyl(4-penten-2-ynyl)amine
hydrobromide
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
