$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical Procedure for the Preparation of the Bromoallene 3a To a solution
of 1a (0.12 g, 0.60 mmol) and Ph3P (0.38 g, 1.4 mmol) in DMF (2.0 mL) was
added CBr4 (0.24 g, 0.72 mmol) at r.t. The solution was stirred at that
temperature for 2 h. The reaction mixture was quenched with H2O (20 mL)
and extracted with hexane-EtOAc (1:1, 3 × 15 mL). Concentration by rotary
evaporator after dried over Na2SO4 furnished a crude mixture that was
purified by silica gel chromatography (hexane-EtOAc, 20:1) to afford 3a.
Pale yellow oil, yield 0.14 g, 0.51 mmol, 85%. Rf = 0.79 (CH2Cl2- EtOAc,
1:1). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 6.71 (q, J = 2.7 Hz, 1 H), 7.34-7.44
(m, 5 H). 13CNMR (75.5 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 82.5 (q, J = 45.3 Hz), 106.8,
119.8 (q, J = 271.7 Hz), 128.5, 129.2, 129.4, 129.9, 202.6 (q, J = 3.1
Hz). 19FNMR (283 MHz, CDCl3): δ = -65.66 (s). IR (neat): 613, 653, 690,
720, 749, 819, 847, 897, 918, 951, 1003, 1029, 1045, 1075, 1119, 1267,
1293, 1313, 1397, 1459, 1496, 1597, 1736, 3034, 3066 cm-1. HRMS-FAB: m/z
calcd for C10H7F3Br [M + H]+: 262.9683; found: 262.9668.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Facile preparation of CF3-containing 1-bromoallenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Watanabe, Yohsuke; Yamazaki, Takashi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2009), (20), 3352-3354

