$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Amberlyst A-26, bromide form, (10 g) is
similarly suspended in a 1.2 normal solution of chlorine in
dichloromethane (100 ml) and shaken overnight. The resin is filtered off,
washed with dichloromethane, dried under reduced pressure, and stored in
a tightly stoppered flask. To estimate the capacity of the reagent, a
sample of the polymer (1.0 g) is extracted with 1 normal aqueous sodium
hydroxide; the iodometric titration of this solution gives a mean value
of 2.5 mmol of halogenating species per gram of reagent 10. Yield: 85 %
(E: 95), Reaction conditions : (solvent/temp/.time): CH2Cl2/r.t./3 h.
b.p. 58-60 °C/0.25 torr.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Anion-exchange resins as halogen carriers in the bromination and
chlorobromination of organic compounds
