$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1,2-dichlorooctane, 5. C60Cl6 (100 mg, 0.107 mmol) was dissolved in 30mL
of 1,1,2,2-tetrachloroethane, followed by the addition of 1 mL of
1-octene to the reaction mixture. The solution was heated to 90°C for 12
hours. Subsequently the reaction was cooled to room temperature and all
volatiles removed. The residue was chromatographed on a silica column
using hexane as the eluent. Yield 16.5 mg, 84%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM C60Cl6, C60Br8 and C60(NO2)6 as selective tools in organic synthesis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Franco, Jimmy U.; Ell, John R.; Hilton, Amanda K.; Hammons, Justin C.;
Olmstead, Marilyn M.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Fullerenes, Nanotubes, and Carbon Nanostructures (2009), 17(4), 349-360

