$DATUM 56-23-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N-(2,3-Dibromopropyl)trifluoromethanesulfonamide (II). Compound I, 5.0 g
(3.7 ml, 0.026 mol), was dissolved in 10 ml of carbon tetrachloride, an
equimolar amount of bromine, 4.2 g (1.35 ml) was added dropwise under
stirring on a magnetic stirrer, and the mixture spontaneously warmed up
to 45°C. The mixture was stirred for 2 h and evaporated under reduced
pressure, the solid residue was ground and dissolved in chloroform, the
solution was washed with water, dried over K2CO3, and evaporated, and the
residue was dried in air. White crystals, yield 7.2 g (84%). mp 39-40°C.
IR spectrum (KBr), ν, cm-1: 3429, 3281, 1451, 1439, 1370, 1230, 1190,
1134, 1059, 989, 837. 1H NMR spectrum, δ, ppm: 3.65 d.d (1H, BrCHA, J =
10.8, 9.8 Hz), 3.69 d.d.d (1H, NCHA, J = 14.6, 6.6, 6.0 Hz), 3.85 d.d
(1H, BrCHB, J = 10.8, 4.3 Hz), 3.95 d.d.d (1H, NCHB, J = 14.6, 6.6, 3.7
Hz), 4.30 m (1H, CHBr), 5.75 br.t (1H, NH, J = 6.5 Hz). 13C NMR spectrum,
δC, ppm: 31.88 (CH2Br), 48.40 (NCH2), 49.40 (CH), 119.60 q (CF3, JCF =
321.0 Hz). 19F NMR spectrum: δF -77.08 ppm. Found, %: C 13.39; H 1.92; Br
45.93; F 17.07; N 3.88; S 9.29. C4H6Br2F3NO2S. Calculated, %: C 13.77; H
1.73; Br 45.80; F 16.30; N 4.01; S 9.19;
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and properties of N-(allyl)trifluoromethanesulfonamide
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Shainyan, B. A.; Danilevich, Yu. S.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Russian Journal of Organic Chemistry (2013), 49(6), 922-923

