$DATUM 1-(2,3-Dibromopropyl)-3-(2-hydroxyethyl)-1H,3H-quinazoline-2,4-dione (3).
A solution of bromine (0.52 ml, 10 mmol) in glacial acetic acid (5 ml)
was added with stirring to a solution of the 1-allylquinazolinedione 2
(2.46 g, 10 mmol) in glacial acetic acid (10 ml). The brown bromine color
disappeared immediately. The reaction mixture was diluted with cold water
and the precipitate was filtered off, washed with cold water, and dried.
Yield 3.37 g (83%). Mp 94-96 °C (EtOH). 1H NMR spectrum, δ, ppm (J, Hz):
8.06 (1H, dd, J= 7.8 andJ= 1.7, H-5); 7.76 (1H, td, J= 7.8 andJ= 1.7,
H-7); 7.53 (1H, d, J= 8.7, H-8); 7.30 (1H, t, J= 7.4, H-6); 4.73 (1H,
quint., J= 6.4, CHBr); 4.60 (2H, m, NCH2CHBr); 4.07 (2H, m, CH2Br); 4.02
(2H, t, J= 6.5, NCH2CH2OH); 3.63 (1H, t, J= 5.9, OH); 3.55 (2H, q, J=
6.5, NCH2CH2OH). 13C NMR spectrum, δ, ppm: 161.7 (4-C═O), 151.2 (2-C═O);
140.2 (C-8a); 135.9 (C-7); 128.8 (C-5); 123.7 (C-6); 115.8 (C-4a); 115.4
(C-8); 58.2 (CH2OH); 50.6 (CHBr); 48.2 ( NCH2CHBr); 43.9 (NCH2CH2OH);
37.0 (CH2Br). Mass spectrum, m/z (Irel, %): 391/389/387 [M-OH]+
(29/58/30), 365/363/361 (20/44/19), 309/307 [M-OH-HBr]+ (80/77), 283/281
(25/27), 227 [M-OH-HBr-HBr]+ (21), 201 (26), 189 (20), 178 (11), 158
(19), 146 (63), 132 (100), 119 (11). Found, %: C 38.33; H 3.37; N 6.98.
C13H14Br2N23 . Calculated, %: C 38.45; H 3.48; 6.90.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM 4-Hydroxy-2-quinolones. 196. Synthesis and bromination of
1-allyl-3-(2-hydroxyethyl)-1H,3H-quinazoline-2,4-dione
