$DATUM 5-Bromo-5-[(bromo)benzyl]-2-methylthio-3-phenyl-3,5-dihydro-4H-imidazol-4-one
(3). A solution of bromine (0.06 g, 0.37 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (10 ml) was
added with stirring at room temperature to a solution of
2-methylthio-5-phenylmethylene-3-phenyl-3,5-dihydro-4H-imidazol-4-one (1)
in methylene chloride (10 ml), stirring was continued for 2 h, monitored
by TLC. Compound 3 (0.12 g, 83%) was obtained as a yellow oil which
crystallized on standing in the air after evaporation of the solvent in
vacuum. Mp 172°C. 1H NMR spectrum (CDCl3), δ, ppm: 7.45 (10H, m, C6H5),
5.94 (1H, s, CHBr), 2.89 (3H, s, SCH3). Found, %: C 45.01; H 3.23; N
6.07. C17H14Br2N2OS. Calculated, %: C 44.90; H 3.08; N 6.16.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A new method for the synthesis of 5-bromo(aryl)methylene-substituted
hydantoins
